![](images/Peranema-41695-2.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Euglenid *Peranema* with algal prey and a stramenopile contaminant."}

![](images/CuF4-1_choano-0333.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Choanoflagellate colony from a salt pond."} 

![](images/LM_chonotrich_small.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Chonotrich ciliate with the closest thing to live birth a protist has -- endogenous bud formation. Epibiont of kelp isopod gills."}

![](images/Biofilm_seq4584-1.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Biofilm with personal spacing"}

![](images/Noctiluca_seq2568-2_YE.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Cytoplasmic channels right beneath the surface of *Noctiluca*"}

![](images/salt-soda-510-2.jpg){width="500px" .lightbox group="LMs" description="Salt crystals (left) and soda crystals (right), visualising the stark chemical difference between sodium chloride dominated neutral pH salt lakes and alkaline soda lakes."}

![](images/Salt_crystal-48873-3.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Pseudo-modernist shot of a salt crystal."}

![](images/BoP3-3_scene-4650-2.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Cyanobacterium and a diatom with its very distant cousin: the brown plastid. They would not recognise each other."}

![](images/CuF2-3U-0127_(c1)-4_YE.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Anaerobic sample microbes with a Dutch Renaissance feel"}

![](images/seq6303-1.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Detail of large empty diatom frustule"}

![](images/seq4764-1_YE.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Two spironemids"}

![](images/Biofilm_seq4584-1.jpg){.lightbox group="LMs" description="Biofilm with personal spacing"}

